<title>ITALY: Italian mutual funds, equity funds post Jan inflow.</title>
<headline>Italian mutual funds, equity funds post Jan inflow.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-02-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Italian investment funds had a net inflow of 18.327 trillion lire in January, compared with a net inflow of 9.177 trillion lire in December, Assogestioni, the industry body said.</p>
<p>It added that equity funds had a net inflow of 1.795 trillion lire in January after a net inflow of 368 billion lire in December.  </p>
<p>The data from Assogestioni on investment funds showed subscriptions at 28.554 trillion lire in January from 15.586 trillion lire in December, while redemptions were 10.227 trillion lire in January from 6.409 trillion lire in December.</p>
<p>It added that total managed assets were 219.000 trillion lire in January from 196.957 trillion lire in December.  </p>
<p>				     January 1997     December 1996</p>
<p> Redemptions (bln lire)	   10,227	     6,409</p>
<p> Subscriptions			28,554	    15,586</p>
<p>Net inflow, outflow (-) from:</p>
<p> Equity funds			  1,795		 368</p>
<p>     of which Italian		  457		  75</p>
<p> Bond funds			   16,144	     8,889</p>
<p> Mixed funds			     388		 -80</p>
<p> Specialised Italy bond funds   10,776	     6,408</p>
